      <title>David Byrne Explains How Forgotten Ideas Come Back to Life</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/audio/2026-10-17/david-byrne-explains-how-forgotten-ideas-come-back-to-life</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">8cf717cb0f1df3e7fcdc4c00</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>History is littered with ideas that have been tossed aside, only for them to gain relevance at some later date. Think of Moby-Dick: forgotten in Melville’s time, but now regarded as the great American novel. Or the work of economist Hyman Minsky, which became influential a decade after his death, when the 2008 financial crisis made “the Minsky Moment”a mainstream term. These are just a couple of the things we talk about with the legendary musician David Byrne on today’s podcast. Byrne’s new book</description>
      <dc:creator>Joe Weisenthal and Tracy Alloway</dc:creator>
